# =============================================================================
# Airpay Academy / Sentientia LMS — Apache .htaccess
# Deploy target: C:\xampp\htdocs\moodle5\public\.htaccess
# (or whichever directory is served as DocumentRoot/Alias for the LMS)
# =============================================================================
#
# Owner: Sentientia LMS Foundation (Day 0, 2026-05-22)
# Bug fix: Goal A audit Bug #7 — raw Apache 404/500/403 pages leak the
# Apache + OpenSSL + PHP version strings AND have zero branding. By
# routing them through Moodle's own error/index.php, learners see the
# branded "404 Error: File not found" page wrapped in the airpayux
# sidebar + footer, instead of the stock Apache page.
#
# Production note: this file is REPO-MANAGED. On every deploy IT must
# copy it to <Moodle public root>/.htaccess. The deploy script under
# moodle-enhancement/deploy/ does this on dev. For production, see the
# IT runbook step "Apply htaccess after pulling production branch".

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Branded error pages
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Route Apache HTTP error codes through Moodle's standard error renderer
# (https://docs.moodle.org/dev/HTTP_error_documents). The /moodle/ prefix
# matches the Apache Alias on this server; for non-aliased deployments
# the path simplifies to /error/index.php.
ErrorDocument 404 /moodle/error/index.php
ErrorDocument 403 /moodle/error/index.php
ErrorDocument 500 /moodle/error/index.php
ErrorDocument 503 /moodle/error/index.php

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Hide Apache server identity in response footer
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ServerSignature controls the "Apache/X.X.X (Win64) OpenSSL/X.X.X
# PHP/X.X.X Server at localhost Port 8080" footer that the default
# Apache 404 page appends. Setting it Off removes the version-string
# leak shown by old-style error pages (security: information disclosure).
#
# NOTE: this only suppresses the FOOTER text. The HTTP `Server:` response
# header is controlled by `ServerTokens` which is NOT allowed in
# .htaccess — it must be set in httpd.conf:
#     ServerTokens Prod
# The IT runbook should set that at the Apache config layer on production.
ServerSignature Off

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. (Existing Moodle defaults you may want — uncomment as needed)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Force HTTPS in production (DON'T enable on local XAMPP — it's HTTP only):
# RewriteEngine On
# RewriteCond %{HTTPS} off
# RewriteRule ^ https://%{HTTP_HOST}%{REQUEST_URI} [L,R=301]

